    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating a new owner's `customerCode` when it collides with an existing owner's code, appending `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n**`OwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 added a `deduplicate(String base, Set<String> existing)` helper (the single source of truth for the code shape), which returns `base` when free, otherwise probes `base-2`, `base-3`, \u2026 and returns the first unused candidate.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the step now injects `OwnerRepository`, collects the existing owners' customer codes, and assigns the de-duplicated result. Its Javadoc was updated to drop the old \"no repository lookup needed\" claim and describe the collision rule. This runs before `assignMembershipNumber`, which derives from `customerCode`, so the membership number naturally inherits the unique value.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` and the full test suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
