    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Pure logic lives in the right unit.** `deduplicate(String base, Set<String> existing)` is a pure, side-effect-free string operation, placed in `OwnerCustomerCode` \u2014 explicitly the \"single source of truth for an owner's `customerCode`.\" It sits naturally alongside `customerCode(...)`, `hash8(...)`, and `region(...)`, matching their static-helper shape and Javadoc style.\n- **I/O lives in the function step.** The repository lookup and the gathering of existing codes stay in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, the function with repository access \u2014 consistent with how other steps (e.g. `Load<E>`) inject and use `OwnerRepository`. The two responsibilities (fetch-the-world vs. compute-the-string) are separated rather than conflated.\n- **No duplication, no catch-all.** Neither class is becoming a grab bag; the new method is a focused addition and the collection loop is short enough to read inline without warranting its own helper.\n- **Docs were updated honestly.** Both Javadocs were revised to drop the now-false \"needs no repository lookup\" claim and describe the collision behavior, so a maintainer isn't misled.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find this a natural place for each piece.",
